	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43922</id><title>Uganda Announces End of Ebola Outbreak, Yet Regional Risks Remain</title><updated>2026-08-28T16:50:26-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43922" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/briefing-reporters-outside_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/briefing-reporters-outside_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/briefing-reporters-outside_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/briefing-reporters-outside_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, August 28 (IPS)  - Following 42 consecutive days without a new confirmed case, The Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention (Africa CDC) and the World Health Organization (WHO) have announced the end of the Ebola outbreak in Uganda.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43922&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Uganda Announces End of Ebola Outbreak, Yet Regional Risks Remain”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43921</id><title>SWEDEN: ‘The New Migration Laws Are so Vague That People Don’t Know What Might Be Used Against Them’</title><updated>2026-08-28T16:34:18-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43921" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/John-Stauffer-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;
CIVICUS discusses Sweden’s new migration laws with John Stauffer, legal director and deputy executive director of Civil Rights Defenders, a Swedish civil society organisation that acts as a civil rights watchdog at home and supports human rights defenders in repressive contexts worldwide.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43921&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “SWEDEN: ‘The New Migration Laws Are so Vague That People Don’t Know What Might Be Used Against Them’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43920</id><title>Family Planning and Population Dynamics Are Key to Water Security</title><updated>2026-08-28T15:56:22-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43920" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Parinacota___.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Parinacota___.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Parinacota___-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Parinacota___.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
OTTAWA, Canada, August 28 (IPS)  - This week is &lt;a href=&quot;https://nationaltoday.com/world-water-week/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;World Water Week&lt;/a&gt;, the annual conference of governments, business, and civil society on building a water-secure future as global population, climate disruptions, and water demand increase.  In Washington, it’s also &lt;a href=&quot;https://transportation.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=410235&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Water Resources Development Act&lt;/a&gt; season, when every two years the US Congress reauthorizes the legilslation that funds US drinking water, wastewater systems, and flood risk management projects.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43920&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Family Planning and Population Dynamics Are Key to Water Security”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43919</id><title>Internally Displaced in Ukraine: Between Hell and a Future That Does Not Exist</title><updated>2026-08-28T10:37:42-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43919" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/internallydisplacedpeopleinukraine1.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/internallydisplacedpeopleinukraine1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/internallydisplacedpeopleinukraine1-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/internallydisplacedpeopleinukraine1.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UZHGOROD, Ukraine, August 28 (IPS)  - It is impossible to ignore. Loudspeakers across the city broadcast a recorded voice announcing a minute’s silence for those who have fallen in the war. After 60 ticks of the second hand, it is time for the national anthem: “Ukraine has not yet perished.”
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43919&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Internally Displaced in Ukraine: Between Hell and a Future That Does Not Exist”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43918</id><title>Consequences of Inaction: UN Security Council Pressed to Act Before Hunger Becomes Famine</title><updated>2026-08-28T08:11:52-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43918" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Lars-Lokke_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Lars-Lokke_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Lars-Lokke_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Lars-Lokke_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, August 28 (IPS)  - Across the board, UN officials and humanitarian organizations urged the Security Council to act before the consequences of food insecurity and famines hit, during a high-level open debate on Tuesday, August 25. More than 80 representatives took part in Tuesday’s conversation on conflict-related food insecurity under the theme “Food under fire: the Security Council’s role in mitigating global and local food crises”.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43918&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Consequences of Inaction: UN Security Council Pressed to Act Before Hunger Becomes Famine”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43913</id><title>Will the Future of the UN be Dictated by a Hostile US?</title><updated>2026-08-28T05:46:42-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43913" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Future-of-the-UN_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Future-of-the-UN_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Future-of-the-UN_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/Future-of-the-UN_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
UNITED NATIONS, August 28 (IPS)  - As the UN commemorates its 81st anniversary, one lingering question remains: what is  the future of the world body? Will a hostile US downsize its operations at the United Nations, cut down its funding, continue defaulting in its payments — and perhaps eventually, withdraw from the world body?
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43913&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Will the Future of the UN be Dictated by a Hostile US?”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43924</id><title>Risks of child recruitment by armed groups rise in post-quake Colombia</title><updated>2026-08-28T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43924" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;The recent earthquake in Colombia could increase the risk of child recruitment by armed groups in Chocó and Valle del Cauca, where thousands of children remain out of school in areas already affected by conflict, the UN warned on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43924&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Risks of child recruitment by armed groups rise in post-quake Colombia”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43923</id><title>‘Immense impact’ of Nepal flood disaster highlighted as casualties mount</title><updated>2026-08-28T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43923" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/27-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/27-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/27-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-03.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/08/27-08-2026-UNICEF-Nepal-floods-03.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The impact of the deadly flood in Nepal has been described as “immense” as the authorities there confirm that 538 bodies have been recovered from the disaster-stricken area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/28/43923&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘Immense impact’ of Nepal flood disaster highlighted as casualties mount”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43910</id><title>U.S. Midwest Flooding Is a Growing Threat to Agriculture</title><updated>2026-08-27T13:36:46-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43910" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/usmidwestflooding.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/usmidwestflooding.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/usmidwestflooding-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/usmidwestflooding.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
