s-and-communities/__;!!DZ3fjg!9bUSxhHh-Okyk1e0ZYb25wXWzEwcVmOhqX--S_ePB1T51MAXTbQe7856h_1_yDy34Xo3SffNsaBDBcVbMA$&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1787920453590000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0wsARQNKjIo3aEbsz8xey7&quot;&gt;Indiana&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43910&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “U.S. Midwest Flooding Is a Growing Threat to Agriculture”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43909</id><title>Fishers’ Organisations in India Demand Recognition From FAO</title><updated>2026-08-27T13:29:02-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43909" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/fishers.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/fishers.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/fishers-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/08/fishers.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
THIRUVANANTHAPURAM, India,, August 27 (IPS)  - India is ranked the second-largest fish-producing nation globally, accounting for around 8 percent of global output. The fisheries sector in India accounts for nearly 7.43 percent of Agricultural Gross Value Added (GVA), the highest (independent) share among the agriculture and allied sectors.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/08/27/43909&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Fishers’ Organisations in India Demand Recognition From FAO”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0009s ch:1 -->